# Planning Ecology Convention
#
# Thin bridge for the site-local agent/editor operating layer.

#>planning_ecology
#:convention #!agents
#:layer #!editor_inspectability

@agents: ~"../../.agents/README.md"
@plans: ~"../../.agents/plans/README.md"
@agent_optimization: ~"../../.agents/plans/agent-optimization/PLAN.md"
@agentic_contracts: ~"../../.agents/plans/agentic-dev-contracts/PLAN.md"
@plan_maintenance: ~"../../.agents/skills/spw-plan-maintenance/SKILL.md"
@public_plans: ~"../../about/plans/index.html"

dispatch: .{
 agents = @agents
 plans = @plans
 agent_optimization = @agent_optimization
 agent_contracts = @agentic_contracts
 plan_maintenance = @plan_maintenance
 public_plans = @public_plans
}[reg=facet]

roles: #[
 `planning ecology`: canonical tracks, active backlog, archive, and public editor projections.
 `agent contracts`: executable validation and manifest contracts that answer whether a change broke the site.
 `skill affordances`: local SKILL.md wrappers that route agents toward site-specific workflows.
 `editor seam`: a route, plan, .spw note, or README that helps a human or agent decide what to do next.
][reg=set]

invariants: #[
 `Site-local plans and skills stay the source of truth for this repository's agent operating layer.`,
 `Public editor pages project the plan ecology; they do not replace the .agents source files.`,
 `New durable planning concepts should be wired through site.spw, this convention, and the relevant README or public page.`,
 `Plan-maintenance sweeps should preserve hand-authored voice while reducing stale cross-references.`
][reg=set]
